[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:SOS]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.24]How did the woman get help? | 那位妇女是怎样获得救助的？
[00:14.45]When a light passenger plane flew off course some time ago, | 不久前，一架轻型客机偏离了航线，
[00:19.68]it crashed in the mountains and its pilot was killed. | 在山区坠落了，飞行员丧生了。
[00:25.25]The only passengers, a young woman and her two baby daughters, were unhurt. | 机上仅有的乘客——一位年轻妇女和她的两个女婴——却安然无恙。
[00:33.51]It was the middle of winter. | 此时正值隆冬季节。
[00:36.08]Snow lay thick on the ground. | 地上积着厚厚的雪。
[00:39.77]The woman knew that the nearest village was miles away. | 这位妇女知道最近的村庄也在数英里之外。
[00:45.05]When it grew dark, she turned a suitcase into a bed and put the children inside it, | 天黑下来时，她把手提箱当作床，把孩子们放了进去，
[00:53.20]covering them with all the clothes she could find. | 又把能找到的衣服都盖在孩子们身上。
[00:57.93]During the night, it got terribly cold. | 夜里天气冷得厉害。
[01:02.47]The woman kept as near as she could to the children and even tried to get into the case herself, but it was too small. | 这位妇女尽可能地靠近孩子们，甚至想自己也挤进箱子里，但箱子太小了。
[01:14.04]Early next morning, | 第二天清晨，
[01:15.79]she heard planes passing overhead and wondered how she could send a signal. | 她听到头顶上有飞机飞过，不知道怎样才能发出信号。
[01:22.70]Then she had an idea. She stamped out the letters 'SOS' in the snow. | 于是她有了一个主意。她在雪地上踩出了“SOS”这三个字母。
[01:31.98]Fortunately, a pilot saw the signal and sent a message by radio to the nearest town. | 幸运的是，一位飞行员看到了这个信号，用无线电给最近的城镇发了报。
[01:40.47]It was not long before a helicopter arrived on the scene to rescue the survivors of the plane crash. | 不久，一架直升机飞到现场，搭救飞机失事的幸存者。
